  "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(y-3)^{2}=2(x+3),\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(y-3)^{2}=2(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nThis is a rightward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(-3,3).$",
